# Five driconf perf options outside TU_FORCE_PROPS: four forced on the released driver, and what the rig cannot see

# Question: this repository searched driver-side speedups through TU_FORCE_PROPS (journal 15) and
#           through env switches (journal 13, 15.5). A surface that search did not cover is the
#           driconf `perf` and `misc` groups: options that change what the command stream does, are
#           NOT in TU_FORCE_PROPS, need no rebuild (an environment variable of the same name
#           overrides them), and are off for our device by default. Four of them are forced in the
#           runs below; the fifth is documented in section 1 because it turns out to be unreachable
#           on a740 without a build:
#             tu_allow_concurrent_binning, tu_disable_conservative_fdm_binning,
#             disable_conservative_lrz, tu_dont_reserve_descriptor_set, (unreachable) tu_independent_icache_miss
#           Is any of the four a regression on the shapes the test rig creates, and is any of them
#           even reachable at all on a740?
# Method:   one test binary, the released driver, five runs; the option forced by an env variable of
#           the same name as the driconf option. The driver confirms each one in its own output
#           ("ATTENTION: default value of option <name> overridden by environment."), which is what
#           proves the run is not a silent no-op.
#           The FULL logs are compared, minus that one line per run.
# Tool:     tests/rp6-vkd3d-sparse-test, sha256 5f44a7f7e6ae... (identical in all five runs)
# Driver:   build/p14-shipped/libvulkan_freedreno.so, sha256 c17d02bcaae9a960...  (the released stack)
# Device:   Adreno A740 (chip_id 0x43050a01), KMD msm
# Runs:     21.11, all five exit 0
# Command:  source scripts/env.sh && RP6_TEST_BIN=/tmp/opencode/testbuild-xmc/rp6-vkd3d-sparse-test \
#               scripts/run-test.sh build/p14-shipped/freedreno_icd_p14.json <log>
#           with <option>=true in the environment for the four forced runs
# Raw:      results/raw/perfprops-{base,tu_allow_concurrent_binning,
#           tu_disable_conservative_fdm_binning,disable_conservative_lrz,
#           tu_dont_reserve_descriptor_set}.log (gitignored)
#
=== 1. what each option is, in the driver's own words, and whether a740 can reach it

  The names below are verbatim from src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_drirc_gen.py, the descriptions are
  the driver's own strings; "read at" is where the value is consumed in the Mesa 27 tree.

  tu_allow_concurrent_binning          group perf
    read at      tu_cmd_buffer.cc:560 (the cache-flush path, gated on CHIP >= A7XX and on
                 !renderpass_cb_disabled), tu_cmd_buffer.cc:3225
                 (tu7_cb_disable_reason(.., "globally disabled")), tu_queue.cc:187 (how many
                 visibility streams the queue reserves)
    also reachable as TU_DEBUG=forcecb / nocb (the names in tu_util.cc:56-57), which
                 overwrite this option after driconf is parsed (tu_device.cc:2083-2086)
    the driver   "Allow concurrent binning on A7XX+, the CB is disabled by default because it
                 regresses performance on desktop games"

  tu_disable_conservative_fdm_binning  group misc
    read at      tu_cmd_buffer.cc:3674 (cons_vis_in_binning, when the pass has_fdm),
                 tu_pipeline.cc:3489 (`return CHIP == A7XX && fdm && !...`)
    the driver   "Don't enable conservative rasterization during binning of a renderpass with
                 FDM, for non-identity FDM tiles may result in tiny see-through gaps in the
                 geometry in places with dense geometry. Improves performance up to 4% on A7XX."

  disable_conservative_lrz             group misc
    read at      tu_lrz.cc:1524 and :1533, where the default (conservative) path calls
                 tu_lrz_disable_write_for_rp(cmd, "Depth write + blending") and
                 (cmd, "Depth write + no color writes"). The option stops the driver from
                 disabling LRZ writes for such a renderpass. The comment above the pair spells
                 out the draw sequence that makes the conservative default necessary, so this
                 one is a correctness trade by construction, not by caution.
    the driver   "Disable conservative LRZ"

  tu_dont_reserve_descriptor_set       group misc
    read at      tu_device.cc:1876 (whether one HW descriptor set is reserved at create)
    the driver   "... this frees up an extra descriptor set at the cost of that feature" (the
                 feature being descriptor set dynamic offsets)

  tu_independent_icache_miss           group perf - NOT REACHABLE on a740
    read at      tu_cmd_buffer.cc:2226 ANDs the option with the prop has_independent_icache_miss,
                 which freedreno_devices.py sets only for FD750/753 (:1341) and
                 freedreno_dev_info.h:408 documents as "A750 only"
                 (SP_CHICKEN_BITS_2.INDEPENDENT_ICACHE_MISS). Env-only would be a silent no-op;
                 asking the hardware needs a build.

=== 2. the runs, compared as text
  run                                     lines  differing lines vs the base run (the ATTENTION line excluded)
  base (no option)                          621  -
  tu_allow_concurrent_binning=true          622  0
  tu_disable_conservative_fdm_binning=true    622  0
  disable_conservative_lrz=true             622  0
  tu_dont_reserve_descriptor_set=true       622  0

  Verdict words are identical too (lines containing each word, over the whole log - not a row
  count; the rows themselves are compared as text by the diff above):
    perfprops-base.log                             EXACT 124  MISMATCH 8   FAIL 6
    perfprops-disable_conservative_lrz.log         EXACT 124  MISMATCH 8   FAIL 6
    perfprops-tu_allow_concurrent_binning.log      EXACT 124  MISMATCH 8   FAIL 6
    perfprops-tu_disable_conservative_fdm_binning.log EXACT 124  MISMATCH 8   FAIL 6
    perfprops-tu_dont_reserve_descriptor_set.log   EXACT 124  MISMATCH 8   FAIL 6
  Each forced run carries exactly one extra line, the driver's own confirmation:
    ATTENTION: default value of option disable_conservative_lrz overridden by environment.
    ATTENTION: default value of option tu_allow_concurrent_binning overridden by environment.
    ATTENTION: default value of option tu_disable_conservative_fdm_binning overridden by environment.
    ATTENTION: default value of option tu_dont_reserve_descriptor_set overridden by environment.

=== 3. what this does and does not say

  It says: none of the four options changes anything the test rig creates - all 621 lines of
  the run, every probe and every readback row, are byte-equal with the option forced.

  It does NOT say they are safe, and it cannot: concurrent binning, conservative FDM binning
  and conservative LRZ all act in a renderpass (binning pass, visibility stream, depth
  resolve). The rig's shapes are image creates, copies, sparse binds, compute reads and
  blits; it has no textured depth renderpass of the kind a game submits. The same gate was
  used for TU_FORCE_PROPS in journal 15 and it was paired there with a picture comparison,
  because "the counter is green" is not a gate (ADR-0006).

  So these three remain UNMEASURED for performance, and unjudged for correctness on real
  rendering. They need the game: a run of scripts/run-game.sh with the option set, the p25
  protocol of journal 15.5 (fps < 30 threshold), and scripts/pixelcheck.py against a base
  screenshot. The game needs about 7 GiB of RAM, which is the whole machine, so the runs are
  queued (docs/plan-next-checks.md queue 12) rather than run here; vkmark, the second rig
  journal 15 used, is no longer installed on this system.
